From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:02:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Use an addon from a folder of the project without
 installing it

xmake loads an addon only from its global addons directory, so a project
which carries an addon in its own tree, e.g. a monorepo with the addon next
to the targets that use it, had to install that folder globally first, and
the install made it the machine's active version for every other project.

add_addons() now takes a sourcedir, relative to the project directory:

    add_addons("revenant", {sourcedir = "toolchain"})

The project uses the addon in that folder as it is, in this process only,
and nothing is installed, locked or activated. Its manifest and payload
root are read as an install reads them (addon.lua, set_sourcedir, the src
layout), and the addon is checked for conflicts like an installed one.

addon.use() records the folder in the addons view of the process, which
overrides an installed version of the same name, and the payload
directories come from addon._rootdir(), so every reference resolves to the
folder: @addon/<name>/<rule|toolchain|include|template>,
import("@addon.<name>.<module>"), @self inside the addon, the global modules
of its manifest, and its plugins. The menu loads the project tasks before
the plugins now, so a plugin of such an addon is a command of the project;
loading the project also pins the versions which its lock names, so a
project which locks another version of an installed addon than the active
one runs the plugins of the locked version too.
The folders are passed on to the child processes in
XMAKE_ADDONS_SOURCEDIRS, so an xmake started by the build, e.g. a package
built with xmake or an on_test script, sees the same addon. The auto-fetch
and `xmake addon --upgrade` leave these declarations out
(addons.installable()). `xmake -v` prints the folder of each one once.

test_sourcedir_addons declares five fixtures by their folders and checks a
rule which imports @self, an includes file, a module import, a toolchain
and a global module of the src layout, a module import in a child xmake,
and a plugin, that nothing is installed or fetched, that the plugin is
gone outside the project, and that a folder holding another addon is
refused. Without the change the project tries to install the fixtures
from the repositories and fails ("package(custom-rule) not found").

Changes-build-output: no

